  "_transitions": "The `transition` row is CSS `transition` (LLP 1002): count u8 (\u22648), then per declaration property u8 (0 all, then 1 + `Property`: 1 translate, 2 scale, 3 rotate, 4 opacity, 5 height, 6 stroke-dashoffset, 7 r, 8 color, 9 background-color, 10 fill, 11 stroke), duration f32 s, delay f32 s, easing u8 (0 linear, 1 ease, 2 ease-in, 3 ease-out, 4 ease-in-out, 5 cubic-bezier + 4\u00d7f32, 6 steps + u16 count + u8 position, 7 spring + f32 stiffness/damping/mass, 8 linear() + u8 count + count\u00d7(f32 input, f32 output)). Its Rust type lives in exact-motion; the kernel owns the bytes.",
  "_animations": "The `animation` row is CSS `animation` (LLP 1055 D5): count u8 (\u22648), then per animation name (str), duration f32 s, delay f32 s, easing (as `_transitions`, never a spring), iteration count f32 (+inf is `infinite`), direction u8 (0 normal, 1 reverse, 2 alternate, 3 alternate-reverse), fill u8 (0 none, 1 forwards, 2 backwards, 3 both), paused u8, then its keyframes: count u8 (\u226432), per keyframe offset f32 in [0,1], easing flag u8 (0 the animation's, 1 followed by an easing), count u8, per value property u8 (as `Property`), then its components as f32: one, two for `translate`, four for a colour (premultiplied sRGB red, green, blue, alpha; LLP 1055.000 D6). Its Rust type lives in exact-motion; the kernel owns the bytes.",
  "_opcodes": "The closed wire-visible op list for EXWF frame revision 1. There is no op count on the wire; consumers iterate by validated lengths.",
